title: A Vote of No Confidence
tags: event
priority: 3
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and months_to_election > 3 and ((govt_type >= 2 and partner_dissent >= 8) or (govt_type = 1 and con_majority < 10 and rebellion >= 8))
new-page: true

= A Vote of No Confidence

[+ lab_leader +] has tabled a motion of no confidence in the government. [? if govt_type = 2 : The Ulster Unionists are threatening to vote with Labour. ?][? if govt_type = 3 : The Liberals say we have broken our side of the bargain. ?][? if govt_type = 4 : Every opposition party could vote together. ?][? if govt_type = 1 : With our majority down to [+ con_majority +], a handful of rebels could bring us down. ?]

- @buy_off: Make whatever concessions it takes.
- @face_it: Face the vote, and dare them.

@buy_off
subtitle: -3 resources
choose-if: resources >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 3 resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 3; partner_dissent = 3; rebellion -= 3; uup_relation += 8 if govt_type = 2; lib_relation += 8 if govt_type = 3; wet_dissent -= 4; budget -= 1

Promises are made in the corridors. The motion is defeated comfortably.

@face_it
on-arrival: {!
var survive = 50 - 4 * (Q.partner_dissent - 6) - 3 * (Q.rebellion - 6) + (Q.thatcher_rating - 35) * 0.5;
Q.survived_confidence = (Math.random() * 100 < survive) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: survived if survived_confidence = 1; fell if survived_confidence = 0

@survived
on-arrival: partner_dissent -= 3; rebellion -= 3; thatcher_rating += 2

The government survives by a handful of votes.

@fell
on-arrival: government_fell = 1; time_to_election = 1; thatcher_rating -= 5
call: set_election

The government is defeated. You go to the Palace to ask for a dissolution. The general election will be held in [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
